From: Modrinth Enhanced <patches@modrinth-enhanced.invalid>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 14:43:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Sign in to Microsoft in the player's own browser

The launcher opened Microsoft's sign-in page in a webview of its own,
which is the one place a player cannot use the tools they use everywhere
else: no password manager, no autofill, no passkeys, and no way to tell
by looking that the page is really Microsoft's.

The browser gets all of it. What it cannot do is hand the code back:
this client id is Minecraft's own, its only registered redirect is a
fixed page on login.live.com, and no loopback address is registered for
it, so there is nothing for the launcher to listen on. The browser
therefore lands on that page with the code in the address, and the
player copies the address over - which is what the new modal asks for,
and what `login_browser_finish` reads the code out of.

Every entry point goes through it, since they all end up at
`AccountsCard.login()`. The webview is still one click away in that
modal for anyone the browser does not work out for.
